findings.body:
**Bound the total interval lines admitted per review.**

`ledgerIntervals` limits each row to `MAX_INTERVAL_LINE` (1,000,000) lines, but no limit applies across rows or across the three scopes. `validateReview` builds `requested`, `input`, and `reviewed` at lines 653-655. `ledgerScope` calls `ledgerIntervals` once per row (line 575), and each call allocates its own `Set`. A record with 100 rows per scope, each `[[1,1000000]]`, can allocate up to 300 million Set entries before the digest check at line 656 runs. The source-identity check at line 648 does not reject this input. A shared line budget across the three builds caps the total allocation.

The default budget belongs on `ledgerIntervals`. When `ledgerScope` passes `undefined`, the per-row default applies. Other `ledgerScope` callers keep their current per-row limit.

